IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa7-ch1.l4: Part 13 Chapter 1, General provisions about resolutions (ss 281 to 287), lines 3717-3785 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (coa7)").
--   JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE: the text says yes, or says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not decide.
--   Tags after a branch: "-- FALSE-kind", "-- NOTHING-kind", "-- FORK Fn" (a fork-register entry),
--   "-- MARGINAL a|b" (a reading for a lawyer, NOTES.md).
-- Facts a witness can state are plain inputs; answers another part computes are inputs named for the
-- answering section (PLAN.md section 4).

§ `Part 13 Chapter 1 -- General provisions about resolutions`

-- ---- s 281 Resolutions ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3719 | 281 Resolutions
-- src:3720 | (1) A resolution of the members (or of a class of members) of a private company must be passed—
-- src:3721 | (a) as a written resolution in accordance with Chapter 2, or
-- src:3722 | (b) at a meeting of the members (to which the provisions of Chapter 3 apply).
@ref s 281(1) Resolutions: private company (src:3719-3722)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed as a written resolution in accordance with Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(1) a private company's resolution is passed in a way this section allows` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution of the members (or of a class of members) of a private company must be passed"
    ELSE IF `the resolution was passed as a written resolution in accordance with Chapter 2`
            OR `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be passed— (a) as a written resolution in accordance with Chapter 2, or (b) at a meeting of the members" -- FORK F1

-- src:3723 | (2) A resolution of the members (or of a class of members) of a public company must be passed at a meeting of the members (to which the provisions of Chapter 3 and, where relevant, Chapter 4 apply).
@ref s 281(2) Resolutions: public company (src:3723)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(2) a public company's resolution is passed in the way this section requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution of the members (or of a class of members) of a public company must be passed"
    ELSE IF `the resolution was passed at a meeting of the members to which Chapter 3 applies`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be passed at a meeting of the members" -- FORK F1

DECLARE `s 281(3) what is required` IS ONE OF
    `s 281(3) an ordinary resolution`
    `s 281(3) the higher majority or unanimity the articles require`

-- src:3724 | (3) Where a provision of the Companies Acts—
-- src:3725 | (a) requires a resolution of a company, or of the members (or a class of members) of a company, and
-- src:3726 | (b) does not specify what kind of resolution is required,
-- src:3727 | what is required is an ordinary resolution unless the company's articles require a higher majority (or unanimity).
@ref s 281(3) Resolutions: the default kind of resolution (src:3724-3727)
GIVEN `the provision requires a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision specifies what kind of resolution is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles require a higher majority or unanimity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 281(3) what is required`
`s 281(3) what the Companies Acts require where the kind of resolution is not specified` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the provision requires a resolution`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a provision of the Companies Acts— (a) requires a resolution of a company"
    ELSE IF `the provision specifies what kind of resolution is required`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) does not specify what kind of resolution is required"
         ELSE IF `the company's articles require a higher majority or unanimity`
              THEN JUST `s 281(3) the higher majority or unanimity the articles require`
              ELSE JUST `s 281(3) an ordinary resolution`

DECLARE `s 281(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 281(4) things done otherwise than by passing a resolution`
    `s 281(4) circumstances in which a resolution is or is not treated as having been passed`
    `s 281(4) cases in which a person is precluded from alleging that a resolution has not been duly passed`
    `s 281(4) another matter`

-- src:3728 | (4) Nothing in this Part affects any enactment or rule of law as to—
-- src:3729 | (a) things done otherwise than by passing a resolution,
-- src:3730 | (b) circumstances in which a resolution is or is not treated as having been passed, or
-- src:3731 | (c) cases in which a person is precluded from alleging that a resolution has not been duly passed.
@ref s 281(4) Resolutions: saving for other law (src:3728-3731)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 281(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(4) this Part leaves any enactment or rule of law on the matter unaffected` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 281(4) things done otherwise than by passing a resolution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 281(4) circumstances in which a resolution is or is not treated as having been passed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 281(4) cases in which a person is precluded from alleging that a resolution has not been duly passed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 281(4) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this Part affects any enactment or rule of law as to— (a) ... (b) ... (c)"

-- ---- s 282 Ordinary resolutions ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- This is the seam answer other parts take as `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution`.
-- src:3733 | (1) An ordinary resolution of the members (or of a class of members) of a company means a resolution that is passed by a simple majority.
@ref s 282(1) Ordinary resolutions (src:3733)
GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282(1) the resolution is an ordinary resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `as a written resolution` THEN `s 282(2) a written resolution is passed by a simple majority` counts
    WHEN `at a meeting on a show of hands` THEN `s 282(3) a resolution passed on a show of hands is passed by a simple majority` counts
    WHEN `at a meeting on a poll` THEN `s 282(4) a resolution passed on a poll is passed by a simple majority` counts

-- The counts a vote produces. For a written resolution the first field is the voting rights of the members
-- who signified agreement and the third is the total voting rights of the eligible members (the second is not
-- read). For a show of hands the fields are the votes cast for and against (the third is not read). For a poll
-- they are the voting rights voted for and against (the third is not read).
DECLARE `s 282 vote count` HAS
    `votes or voting rights in favour` IS A NUMBER
    `votes or voting rights against` IS A NUMBER
    `total voting rights of eligible members` IS A NUMBER

-- "Simple majority" is not defined in the Act: taken as more than one half (fork F2).
-- src:3734 | (2) A written resolution is passed by a simple majority if it is passed by members representing a simple majority of the total voting rights of eligible members (see Chapter 2).
@ref s 282(2) Ordinary resolutions: written resolution (src:3734)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282(2) a written resolution is passed by a simple majority` MEANS
    IF counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN counts's `total voting rights of eligible members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is passed by a simple majority if it is passed by members representing a simple majority of the total voting rights of eligible members" -- FORK F2 -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3735 | (3) A resolution passed at a meeting on a show of hands is passed by a simple majority if it is passed by a simple majority of the votes cast by those entitled to vote
@ref s 282(3) Ordinary resolutions: show of hands (src:3735)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282(3) a resolution passed on a show of hands is passed by a simple majority` MEANS
    IF counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` TIMES 2
         GREATER THAN counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` PLUS counts's `votes or voting rights against`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is passed by a simple majority if it is passed by a simple majority of the votes cast by those entitled to vote" -- FORK F2 -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3736 | (4) A resolution passed on a poll taken at a meeting is passed by a simple majority if it is passed by members representing a simple majority of the total voting rights of members who (being entitled to do so) vote in person, by proxy or in advance (see section 322A) on the resolution.
@ref s 282(4) Ordinary resolutions: poll (src:3736)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282(4) a resolution passed on a poll is passed by a simple majority` MEANS
    IF counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` TIMES 2
         GREATER THAN counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` PLUS counts's `votes or voting rights against`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is passed by a simple majority if it is passed by members representing a simple majority of the total voting rights of members who (being entitled to do so) vote" -- FORK F2 -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3737 | (5) Anything that may be done by ordinary resolution may also be done by special resolution.
@ref s 282(5) Ordinary resolutions: a special resolution may do what an ordinary one may (src:3737)
GIVEN `the thing may be done by ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282(5) the thing may also be done by special resolution` MEANS
    IF `the thing may be done by ordinary resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Anything that may be done by ordinary resolution may also be done by special resolution"

-- ---- s 283 Special resolutions ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- This is the seam answer other parts take as `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`.
-- src:3739 | (1) A special resolution of the members (or of a class of members) of a company means a resolution passed by a majority of not less than 75%.
@ref s 283(1) Special resolutions (src:3739)
GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(1) the resolution is a special resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `as a written resolution` THEN `s 283(2) a written resolution is passed by a majority of not less than 75%` counts
    WHEN `at a meeting on a show of hands` THEN `s 283(4) a resolution passed on a show of hands is passed by a majority of not less than 75%` counts
    WHEN `at a meeting on a poll` THEN `s 283(5) a resolution passed on a poll is passed by a majority of not less than 75%` counts

-- src:3740 | (2) A written resolution is passed by a majority of not less than 75% if it is passed by members representing not less than 75% of the total voting rights of eligible members (see Chapter 2).
@ref s 283(2) Special resolutions: written resolution (src:3740)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(2) a written resolution is passed by a majority of not less than 75%` MEANS
    IF counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` TIMES 4 AT LEAST counts's `total voting rights of eligible members` TIMES 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is passed by a majority of not less than 75% if it is passed by members representing not less than 75% of the total voting rights of eligible members" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3744 | (4) A resolution passed at a meeting on a show of hands is passed by a majority of not less than 75% if it is passed by not less than 75% of the votes cast by those entitled to vote.
@ref s 283(4) Special resolutions: show of hands (src:3744)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(4) a resolution passed on a show of hands is passed by a majority of not less than 75%` MEANS
    IF counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` TIMES 4
         AT LEAST (counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` PLUS counts's `votes or voting rights against`) TIMES 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is passed by a majority of not less than 75% if it is passed by not less than 75% of the votes cast by those entitled to vote" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3745 | (5) A resolution passed on a poll taken at a meeting is passed by a majority of not less than 75% if it is passed by members representing not less than 75% of the total voting rights of the members who (being entitled to do so) vote in person, by proxy or in advance (see section 322A) on the resolution.
@ref s 283(5) Special resolutions: poll (src:3745)
GIVEN counts IS A `s 282 vote count`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(5) a resolution passed on a poll is passed by a majority of not less than 75%` MEANS
    IF counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` TIMES 4
         AT LEAST (counts's `votes or voting rights in favour` PLUS counts's `votes or voting rights against`) TIMES 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is passed by a majority of not less than 75% if it is passed by members representing not less than 75% of the total voting rights of the members who (being entitled to do so) vote" -- MARGINAL a

-- "Where a resolution of a private company is passed as a written resolution": the bar. TRUE says the bar holds
-- (the resolution is not a special resolution); FALSE says the text does not bar it (it stated that it was
-- proposed as a special resolution, or the "Where" condition fails).
-- src:3741 | (3) Where a resolution of a private company is passed as a written resolution—
-- src:3742 | (a) the resolution is not a special resolution unless it stated that it was proposed as a special resolution, and
@ref s 283(3)(a) Special resolutions: written resolution of a private company (src:3741-3742)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution stated that it was proposed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(3)(a) the written resolution of the private company is not a special resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` OR (NOT `the resolution was passed as a written resolution`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a resolution of a private company is passed as a written resolution—" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the resolution stated that it was proposed as a special resolution`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a special resolution unless it stated that it was proposed as a special resolution" -- FORK F3
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3743 | (b) if the resolution so stated, it may only be passed as a special resolution.
@ref s 283(3)(b) Special resolutions: written resolution stated to be special (src:3743)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was passed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution stated that it was proposed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(3)(b) the written resolution may only be passed as a special resolution` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` OR (NOT `the resolution was passed as a written resolution`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a resolution of a private company is passed as a written resolution—" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the resolution stated that it was proposed as a special resolution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the resolution so stated, it may only be passed as a special resolution" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3747 | (a) the resolution is not a special resolution unless the notice of the meeting included the text of the resolution and specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution, and
@ref s 283(6)(a) Special resolutions: resolution passed at a meeting (src:3747)
GIVEN `the resolution was passed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of the meeting included the text of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of the meeting specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(6)(a) the resolution passed at the meeting is not a special resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the resolution was passed at a meeting`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a resolution is passed at a meeting—" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the notice of the meeting included the text of the resolution`
            AND `the notice of the meeting specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a special resolution unless the notice of the meeting included the text of the resolution and specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution" -- FORK F3
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3748 | (b) if the notice of the meeting so specified, the resolution may only be passed as a special resolution.
@ref s 283(6)(b) Special resolutions: notice specified a special resolution (src:3748)
GIVEN `the resolution was passed at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of the meeting specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(6)(b) the resolution passed at the meeting may only be passed as a special resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the resolution was passed at a meeting`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a resolution is passed at a meeting—" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the notice of the meeting specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the notice of the meeting so specified, the resolution may only be passed as a special resolution" -- MARGINAL a

-- ---- s 284 Votes: general rules ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "(4) The provisions of this section have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles."
-- src:3757 | (4) The provisions of this section have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles.
@ref s 284(4) Votes: general rules, subject to the articles (src:3757)
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 284(4) the rules of this section have effect` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this section have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F4 -- MARGINAL b
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- One vote for each share or each £10 of stock held: the votes are the shares plus the whole tens of pounds of stock.
-- src:3750 | (1) On a vote on a written resolution—
-- src:3751 | (a) in the case of a company having a share capital, every member has one vote in respect of each share or each £10 of stock held by him, and
-- src:3752 | (b) in any other case, every member has one vote.
@ref s 284(1) Votes: general rules, written resolution (src:3750-3752)
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `shares held by the member` IS A NUMBER
      `pounds of stock held by the member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 284(1) the member's votes on a written resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 284(4) the rules of this section have effect` `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the number of votes is then fixed by the company's articles
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the company has a share capital`
        THEN JUST (`shares held by the member` PLUS FLOOR (`pounds of stock held by the member` DIVIDED BY 10))
        ELSE JUST 1

-- src:3753 | (2) On a vote on a resolution on a show of hands at a meeting, each member present in person has one vote.
@ref s 284(2) Votes: general rules, show of hands (src:3753)
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is present in person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 284(2) the member's votes on a show of hands` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 284(4) the rules of this section have effect` `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the number of votes is then fixed by the company's articles
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the member is present in person`
        THEN JUST 1
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each member present in person has one vote"

-- src:3754 | (3) On a vote on a resolution on a poll taken at a meeting—
-- src:3755 | (a) in the case of a company having a share capital, every member has one vote in respect of each share or each £10 of stock held by him, and
-- src:3756 | (b) in any other case, every member has one vote.
@ref s 284(3) Votes: general rules, poll (src:3754-3756)
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `shares held by the member` IS A NUMBER
      `pounds of stock held by the member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 284(3) the member's votes on a poll` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 284(4) the rules of this section have effect` `the articles contain a provision on the number of votes`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the number of votes is then fixed by the company's articles
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the company has a share capital`
        THEN JUST (`shares held by the member` PLUS FLOOR (`pounds of stock held by the member` DIVIDED BY 10))
        ELSE JUST 1

DECLARE `s 284(5) saved section` IS ONE OF
    `s 284(5) section 152 (exercise of rights by nominees)`
    `s 284(5) section 285 (voting by proxy)`
    `s 284(5) section 322 (exercise of voting rights on poll)`
    `s 284(5) section 322A (voting on a poll: votes cast in advance)`
    `s 284(5) section 323 (representation of corporations at meetings)`
    `s 284(5) another section`

-- src:3758 | (5) Nothing in this section is to be read as restricting the effect of—
-- src:3759 | section 152 (exercise of rights by nominees),
-- src:3760 | section 285 (voting by proxy),
-- src:3761 | section 322 (exercise of voting rights on poll),
-- src:3762 | section 322A (voting on a poll: votes cast in advance), or
-- src:3763 | section 323 (representation of corporations at meetings).
@ref s 284(5) Votes: general rules, saving (src:3758-3763)
GIVEN section IS A `s 284(5) saved section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 284(5) this section is not to be read as restricting the effect of the section` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `s 284(5) another section` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section is to be read as restricting the effect of— section 152 ... or section 323"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 285 Voting by proxy ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3765 | (1) On a vote on a resolution on a show of hands at a meeting, every proxy present who has been duly appointed by one or more members entitled to vote on the resolution has one vote. This is subject to subsection (2).
@ref s 285(1) Voting by proxy: show of hands (src:3765)
GIVEN `the proxy is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proxy has been duly appointed by one or more members entitled to vote on the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 285(1) the proxy's votes on a show of hands` MEANS
    IF `the proxy is present` AND `the proxy has been duly appointed by one or more members entitled to vote on the resolution`
    THEN JUST 1
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every proxy present who has been duly appointed by one or more members entitled to vote on the resolution has one vote"

-- src:3766 | (2) On a vote on a resolution on a show of hands at a meeting, a proxy has one vote for and one vote against the resolution if—
-- src:3767 | (a) the proxy has been duly appointed by more than one member entitled to vote on the resolution, and
-- src:3768 | (b) the proxy has been instructed by one or more of those members to vote for the resolution and by one or more other of those members to vote against it.
@ref s 285(2) Voting by proxy: one vote for and one against (src:3766-3768)
GIVEN `members who duly appointed the proxy and are entitled to vote on the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote for the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote against the resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 285(2) the proxy has one vote for and one vote against the resolution` MEANS
    IF `members who duly appointed the proxy and are entitled to vote on the resolution` GREATER THAN 1
        AND `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote for the resolution` AT LEAST 1
        AND `of those members, the number who instructed the proxy to vote against the resolution` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a proxy has one vote for and one vote against the resolution if—" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3769 | (3) On a poll taken at a meeting of a company all or any of the voting rights of a member may be exercised by one or more duly appointed proxies.
@ref s 285(3) Voting by proxy: poll (src:3769)
GIVEN `the proxy has been duly appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 285(3) the member's voting rights on a poll may be exercised by the proxy` MEANS
    IF `the proxy has been duly appointed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be exercised by one or more duly appointed proxies"

-- src:3770 | (4) Where a member appoints more than one proxy, subsection (3) does not authorise the exercise by the proxies taken together of more extensive voting rights than could be exercised by the member in person.
@ref s 285(4) Voting by proxy: proxies together (src:3770)
GIVEN `the member appoints more than one proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `voting rights the proxies exercise taken together` IS A NUMBER
      `voting rights the member could exercise in person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 285(4) subsection (3) authorises the proxies together to exercise these rights` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the member appoints more than one proxy`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a member appoints more than one proxy" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `voting rights the proxies exercise taken together` GREATER THAN `voting rights the member could exercise in person`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (3) does not authorise the exercise by the proxies taken together of more extensive voting rights than could be exercised by the member in person"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (4) says only what subsection (3) does not authorise

-- src:3771 | (5) Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles.
@ref s 285(5) Voting by proxy: subject to the articles (src:3771)
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the matters in subsections (1) and (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 285(5) subsections (1) and (2) have effect` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain a provision on the matters in subsections (1) and (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F4 -- MARGINAL b
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 285A Voting rights on poll or written resolution ---------------------------------------------------

-- The number of votes a member has on a poll is void where a private company's articles give a different number
-- on a poll and on a written resolution, for a resolution required or authorised by an enactment; the member
-- then has the same number on the poll as on the written resolution.
-- src:3773 | In relation to a resolution required or authorised by an enactment, if a private company's articles provide that a member has a different number of votes in relation to a resolution when it is passed as a written resolution and when it is passed on a poll taken at a meeting—
-- src:3774 | (a) the provision about how many votes a member has in relation to the resolution passed on a poll is void, and
-- src:3775 | (b) a member has the same number of votes in relation to the resolution when it is passed on a poll as the member has when it is passed as a written resolution.
@ref s 285A Voting rights on poll or written resolution (src:3773-3775)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is required or authorised by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles give a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `votes the member has on the written resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 285A the member's votes on a poll` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` OR (NOT `the resolution is required or authorised by an enactment`)
        OR (NOT `the articles give a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a resolution required or authorised by an enactment, if a private company's articles provide that a member has a different number of votes"
    ELSE JUST `votes the member has on the written resolution`

@ref s 285A(a) and (b) Voting rights on poll or written resolution: void (src:3774-3775)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is required or authorised by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles give a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 285A(a) the articles' provision about votes on a poll is void` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` OR (NOT `the resolution is required or authorised by an enactment`)
        OR (NOT `the articles give a different number of votes on a poll and on a written resolution`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a private company's articles provide that a member has a different number of votes" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 286 Votes of joint holders of shares ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- The senior holder who votes: the first, in the order of the register of members, among the holders who vote.
-- src:3778 | (2) For the purposes of this section, the senior holder of a share is determined by the order in which the names of the joint holders appear in the register of members ....
@ref s 286(2) Votes of joint holders: the senior holder (src:3778)
GIVEN `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `joint holders who vote` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 286(2) the senior holder who votes` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN holder YIELD elem holder `joint holders who vote`) `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no joint holder votes, so there is no senior holder who votes
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST first

-- src:3777 | (1) In the case of joint holders of shares of a company, only the vote of the senior holder who votes (and any proxies duly authorised by him) may be counted by the company.
@ref s 286(1) Votes of joint holders: only the senior holder's vote counts (src:3777)
GIVEN `the holder whose vote is in question` IS A STRING
      `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `joint holders who vote` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286(1) the holder's own vote may be counted by the company` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F4
    ELSE IF (NOT (elem `the holder whose vote is in question` `joint holders who vote`))
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the holder did not vote
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 286(2) the senior holder who votes` `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members` `joint holders who vote`
              WHEN JUST senior THEN
                  IF senior EQUALS `the holder whose vote is in question`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only the vote of the senior holder who votes (and any proxies duly authorised by him) may be counted by the company"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no joint holder votes

@ref s 286(1) Votes of joint holders: proxies of the senior holder (src:3777)
GIVEN `the proxy is duly authorised by the holder` IS A STRING
      `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `joint holders who vote` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286(1) a vote by a proxy duly authorised by the holder may be counted by the company` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F4
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 286(2) the senior holder who votes` `joint holders in the order their names appear in the register of members` `joint holders who vote`
         WHEN JUST senior THEN
             IF senior EQUALS `the proxy is duly authorised by the holder`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only the vote of the senior holder who votes (and any proxies duly authorised by him) may be counted by the company"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no joint holder votes

-- src:3779 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles.
@ref s 286(3) Votes of joint holders: subject to the articles (src:3779)
GIVEN `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286(3) subsections (1) and (2) have effect` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain a provision on the votes of joint holders`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F4 -- MARGINAL b
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 287 Saving for provisions of articles as to determination of entitlement to vote -------------------

DECLARE `s 287 matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 287(a) a provision of the articles requiring an objection to a person's entitlement to vote to be made in accordance with the articles and for its determination to be final and conclusive`
    `s 287(b) the grounds on which such a determination may be questioned in legal proceedings`
    `s 287 another matter`

-- src:3781 | Nothing in this Chapter affects—
-- src:3782 | (a) any provision of a company's articles—
-- src:3783 | (i) requiring an objection to a person's entitlement to vote on a resolution to be made in accordance with the articles, and
-- src:3784 | (ii) for the determination of any such objection to be final and conclusive, or
-- src:3785 | (b) the grounds on which such a determination may be questioned in legal proceedings.
@ref s 287 Saving for provisions of articles as to determination of entitlement to vote (src:3781-3785)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 287 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 287 this Chapter leaves the matter unaffected` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 287(a) a provision of the articles requiring an objection to a person's entitlement to vote to be made in accordance with the articles and for its determination to be final and conclusive` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 287(b) the grounds on which such a determination may be questioned in legal proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 287 another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this Chapter affects— (a) ... (b) ..."
